(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA) '
(NATIONAL HEALTH AUTHORITY [NHA] & MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE) '
T*
(AYUSHMAN BHARAT - PRADHAN MANTRI JAN AROGYA YOJANA [AB-PMJAY]) '
T*
(1. SCHEME OBJECTIVE AND SCOPE) '
(Ayushman Bharat PM-JAY is the world's largest government-funded healthcare assurance ) '
(scheme, launched in September 2018. It aims to provide universal health coverage and ) '
(financial protection to over 12 crore vulnerable rural and urban families [approx 55 ) '
(crore beneficiaries], representing the bottom 40% of the Indian population. In 2024, ) '
(the scheme expanded to cover all senior citizens aged 70 years and above irrespective ) '
(of their income status.) '
T*
(2. HEALTH COVERAGE AND BENEFIT PACKAGE) '
(- Health Cover: ?5,00,000 [Rupees Five Lakh] per family per year for secondary and ) '
(tertiary care hospitalization across all empaneled public and private hospitals ) '
(nationwide.) '
(- Cashless and Paperless Access: 100% cashless treatment at the point of care.) '
(- Pre and Post-Hospitalization: Covers up to 3 days of pre-hospitalization and 15 ) '
(days of post-hospitalization diagnostic and medication expenses.) '
(- Over 1,949 medical and surgical procedures covered, including oncology, cardiology, ) '
(neurosurgery, and intensive care treatments.) '
(- No restriction on family size, age, or gender. Pre-existing medical conditions are ) '
(covered from day one of enrollment.) '
T*
(3. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA) '
(- Beneficiaries identified automatically based on deprivation and occupational ) '
(criteria in the Socio-Economic and Caste Census [SECC 2011] database and National ) '
(Food Security Act [NFSA] ration cards.) '
(- All senior citizens aged 70 years and above are eligible for dedicated ) '
(Top-Up/Ayushman cards regardless of economic category.) '
T*
(4. AYUSHMAN CARD CREATION & REQUIRED DOCUMENTS) '
(- Aadhaar Card [mandatory for identity verification].) '
(- Ration Card / Family ID document.) '
(- Mobile Number for e-KYC.) '
(Citizens can check eligibility and download their Ayushman Card [Golden Card] through ) '
(the Ayushman App or the official portal at https://beneficiary.nha.gov.in.) '
T*
(5. IMPLEMENTING AGENCY AND CONTACT HELPLINE) '
(- Central Nodal Body: National Health Authority [NHA], Government of India.) '
(- State Implementing Body: State Health Agencies [SHA].) '
(- National Toll-Free Helpline: 14555.) '
(- Official Website: https://nha.gov.in / https://pmjay.gov.in.) '
ET
